sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To draw a straight line through a given point parallel to a given straight line.
----
proof:

Let {A} be the given point, and {BC} the given straight line.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="160" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.31 diagram" src="propI31.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "I.31",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;130,40",
            "B;point;free;40,120",
            "C;point;free;180,120",
            "D;point;lineSlider;B,C,100,120",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "AE;line;similar;A,D,D,A,C",
            "E;point;last;AE",
            "AF;line;extend;E,A,B,D",
            "F;point;last;AF",
            // Zero-color hover target for the whole constructed parallel
            // E–A–F (so {EF} / {EAF} light the full line through A; it is
            // drawn visibly as AE + AF).
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            // The alternate angles AD makes (#91): the copied ∠EAD (=∠DAE) at
            // A and the original ∠ADC at D. Distinct vertices, no #103 nesting.
            "EAD;sector;angleMarker;A,E,D",
            "ADC;sector;angleMarker;D,A,C"
        ],
        aliases: { "DAE": "EAD", "EAF": "EF" },
        deferDraggables: ["D"],
        slides: [
            { text: "Let {A} be the given point, and {BC} the given straight line.",
              visible: ["BC"],
              highlighted: ["A","BC"] },
            { text: "It is required to draw a straight line through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC"],
              highlighted: ["A","BC"] },
            { text: "Take a point {D} at random on {BC}. Join {AD}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD"],
              highlighted: ["D","AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "D",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Construct the angle {DAE} equal to the angle {ADC} on the straight line {DA} and at the point {A} on it.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD"],
              highlighted: ["EAD","ADC","AE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "ADC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "AE",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "EAD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "Produce the straight line {AF} in a straight line with {EA}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F"],
              highlighted: ["AF"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "AF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Since the straight line {AD} falling on the two straight lines {BC} and {EF} makes the alternate angles {EAD} and {ADC} equal to one another, therefore {EAF} is parallel to {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F","EF"],
              highlighted: ["AD","BC","EF","EAD","ADC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.27" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the straight line {EAF} has been drawn through the given point {A} parallel to the given straight line {BC}.",
              visible: ["BC","D","AD","AE","E","ADC","EAD","AF","F","EF"],
              highlighted: ["EF","A","BC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.2": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "I.23":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.27":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI27/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to draw a straight line through the point {A} parallel to the straight line {BC}.

Take a point {D} at random on {BC}. Join {AD}. Construct the angle {DAE} equal to the angle {ADC} on the straight line {DA} and at the point {A} on it. Produce the straight line {AF} in a straight line with {EA}. [!just I.Post.1; I.23; I.Post.2]

Since the straight line {AD} falling on the two straight lines {BC} and {EF} makes the alternate angles {EAD} and {ADC} equal to one another, therefore {EAF} is parallel to {BC}. [!just I.27]

Therefore the straight line {EAF} has been drawn through the given point {A} parallel to the given straight line {BC}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide:

The parallel line {EF} constructed in this proposition is the only one passing through the point {A}. If there were another, then the interior angles on one side or the other of {AD} it makes with {BC} would be less than two right angles, and therefore by the parallel postulate @I.Post.5, it would meet {BC}, a contradiction.

Incidentally, this construction also works in hyperbolic geometry, although different parallel lines through {A} are constructed for different points {D}.

#### Construction steps

The construction needed is that of @I.23 to construct an angle. That construction required ten circles and one line in general. In the specific case needed here, however, one of the distances does not have to be transferred, and that eliminates the need to construct four of the circles. Therefore this construction actually only requires six circles and a line.

The walk below carries out that specialized copy of the angle, and counts the six circles at the end.

<figure class="diagram rdiagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="360" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.31 six-circle construction" src="propI31.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_1",
        background: "0,0,100",
        title: "I.31 — six circles",
        elements: [
            "D;point;free;110,200",
            "A;point;free;190,70",
            "C;point;free;260,200",
            // The given angle ADC (vertex D), and the line AD it is copied onto.
            "sideDA;line;connect;D,A;0;0;black",
            "sideDC;line;connect;D,C;0;0;black",
            "ADC;sector;angleMarker;D,A,C",
            // Apollonius "equal-sides" circle (centre D, radius DA): meets DC at
            // P so DP = DA — like I.23's Ccirc, it is the uncounted extra circle
            // that lets only ONE further distance be transferred.
            "Dcirc;circle;radius;D,A;0;0;black;0",
            "P;point;cutoff;D,C,D,A",
            "AP;line;connect;A,P;0;0;0",
            // The six counted circles: Acirc (centre A through D — the side DA is
            // already in place, so no transfer scaffolding) + the chord-transfer
            // of AP to centre D (its 4 kept circles gKa/gKc/gKc2/gKT) + Gcirc.
            "Acirc;circle;radius;A,D;0;0;black;0",
            "Gcirc;circle;radius;D,A,P;0;0;black;0",
            "E'E;line;bichord;Acirc,Gcirc;0;0",
            "E;point;first;E'E",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E",
            "DAE;sector;angleMarker;A,D,E"
        ],
        slides: [
            { text: "The construction is that of {ADC}, copied. We copy the given angle {ADC} at {D} onto the line {AD} at the point {A}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC"],
              highlighted: ["ADC"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "ADC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "First make the two sides equal: with centre {D} and radius {DA}, draw a circle. It meets {DC} at {P}, so {DP} equals {DA}. (As Apollonius noted, this one circle lets only one further distance be transferred.)",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC","Dcirc","P"],
              highlighted: ["Dcirc","P"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "Dcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "P",     name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Along the line {AD} the side {DA} is already in place — laying it off from {A} lands back on {D}, so that distance is not transferred, saving four circles. Draw the circle with centre {A} through {D}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC","P","Acirc"],
              highlighted: ["Acirc"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "Acirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "Transfer the chord {AP} to the centre {D}: one compass-transfer walk lays it off, leaving the circle with centre {D} and radius {AP}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC","P","Acirc","AP","Gcirc"],
              highlighted: ["Gcirc","AP"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "Gcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compassTransfer,
                    args: { side: 1, keepCircles: ["gKa","gKc","gKc2","gKT"] } } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.1" }, { ref: "I.2" }] },
            { text: "The two circles meet at {E}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC","P","Acirc","Gcirc","E"],
              highlighted: ["Acirc","Gcirc","E"],
              transition: { animations: [ { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Join {AE}. The angle {DAE} equals the given angle {ADC} — and {AE} gives the direction of the parallel.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","ADC","P","Acirc","Gcirc","E","AE","DAE"],
              highlighted: ["DAE","ADC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AE",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DAE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "In all there are six circles and one line: the circle on {A}, the four of the chord-transfer, and the circle on {D}.",
              visible: ["sideDA","sideDC","E","AE","Acirc","gKa","gKc","gKc2","gKT","Gcirc"],
              highlighted: ["AE","Acirc","gKa","gKc","gKc2","gKT","Gcirc"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AE",    name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "Acirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "gKa",   name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "gKc",   name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "gKc2",  name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "gKT",   name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "Gcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.1": "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI1/",
        "I.2": "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI2/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

#### Use of Proposition 31

This construction is frequently used in the remainder of Book I starting with the next proposition. It is also frequently used in Books II, IV, VI, XI, XII, and XIII.
